# Everything the Marketplace package does not need. The published .vsix should
# be the bundle, the icon and the two documents a reader looks for — nothing
# that would let someone mistake the package for the source of truth.
src/**
tools/**
node_modules/**
.vscode/**
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.ts
package-lock.json
**/*.test.ts

# The sourcemap ships on purpose. The bundle is minified, so without it every
# stack trace in a bug report is unreadable — a few hundred KB is a cheap price
# for being able to act on the reports that do arrive.

# The tokenizer, and only the parts of it that are used.
#
# `tools/build.ts` marks these external so the encoder stays a lazy runtime
# require rather than 3.3 MB inlined into the bundle. That only works if the
# files are actually in the package, so these four negations are load-bearing:
# remove one and exact token counting silently degrades to a calibrated ratio.
#
# `package.json` is needed for the exports map that resolves the subpaths, and
# the `require` condition is what selects the .cjs files rather than the .js
# ones. The other five rank tables — gpt2, p50k, p50k_edit, r50k — stay
# excluded; no model in the catalog uses them, and together they are 7 MB.
!node_modules/js-tiktoken/package.json
!node_modules/js-tiktoken/dist/lite.cjs
!node_modules/js-tiktoken/dist/ranks/o200k_base.cjs
!node_modules/js-tiktoken/dist/ranks/cl100k_base.cjs
